# Reviewing changes in `meta/`

The unified reviewer (`prompts/codeReviewer/v3/`) loads **`meta/REVIEW.md`** for any
changed path under `meta/`. That map cites rule IDs from `meta/AGENTS.md` (e.g. `AP-4`,
`AP-6`, `TAP-4`) — it never restates the rule text.

Deterministic checks that fire here first (precedence over LLM):
- D1 dependency table (`check_dependency_rules`) — meta must not import from
  `orchestration/` (AP-4: meta reads logs/config, never calls the graph).
- D5 AP-6 — no fabricated metrics (`None` not `0.0`) (LLM-judged).
- D3 TAP-4 (`detect_failure_path_ratio`) on `tests/meta/**` — failure-path ratio per
  decision point (rule content localized to `meta/AGENTS.md §L4`, P2-11).

Dispatch the reviewer:

```bash
python -m meta.code_reviewer --from-git-diff --git-base HEAD --prompt-version v3 --output review.json
```

Deterministic findings are the gate; the v3 LLM judge is WI-8 certified (TPR/TNR = 1.0) so LLM verdicts are gate-grade for the routed LLM-only rules — re-record when the judge model changes.
Full contract: `docs/skills/code-review/SKILL.md`.
